                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+system"} weight system
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+weight+system"} horizontal weight system
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+knot+invariant"} Vassiliev knot invariant
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+braid+invariant"} Vassiliev braid invariant
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems+are+associated+graded+of+Vassiliev+invariants"} weight systems are associated graded of Vassiliev invariants
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+weight+systems+are+cohomology+of+loop+space+of+configuration+space"} horizontal weight systems are cohomology of loop space of configuration space
          %h3#AtiyahSutcliffeConstruction Berry-Robbins and Atiyah-Sutcliffe construction
          %p
            In the course of providing a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-statistics+theorem"} spin-statistics theorem
            %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#BerryRobbins97"} Berry &amp; Robbins 1997
            asked, at each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
            and
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sym
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+function"} equivariant function
          #eq:TheBerryRobbinsMap.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (19)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi Conf
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{ {}^{\{1,\cdots, n\}}  }{Conf}\big(\mathbb{R}^3\big)
                  \\xrightarrow{\phantom{AAA}}
                  \\mathrm{U}(n)/\big(\mathrm{U}(1)\big)^n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                from the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"}
                  configuration space of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  points
                (ordered and unlabeled) in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
            %li
              %p
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{U}(n)
                by its
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+manifold"} flag manifold
                of flags in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n
          %p
            both equipped with the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} group action
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
          %p
            For the first non-empty case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            this readily reduces to asking for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \setminus \{0\} \xrightarrow{\;\;} \mathbb{C}P^1 \simeq S^2
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+function"} equivariant
            with respect to passage to antipodal points. This is immediately seen to be given by the radial projection. But this special case turns out not to be representative of the general case, as this simple construction idea does not generalize to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 2
          %p
            That a continuous and
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheBerryRobbinsMap"} (19)
            indeed exists for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            was proven in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#Atiyah00"} Atiyah 2000
          %p
            In this article,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"} Atiyah
            turned attention to the stronger question asking for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(n) \times
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%283%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant"} equivariant
            function
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheBerryRobbinsMap"} (19)
            and provided an elegant proof strategy for this stronger statement, which however hinges on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectural
            positivity properties of a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            (discussed in more detail and with first numerical evidence in
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#Atiyah01"} Atiyah 2001
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electrostatic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particles"} particles
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
          %p
            Extensive numerical checks of this stronger but conjectural construction was recorded, up to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn 30
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \lt 30
            , in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#AtiyahSutcliffe02"} Atiyah &amp; Sutcliffe 2002
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecture
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture"} Atiyah-Sutcliffe conjecture
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture"} Atiyah-Sutcliffe conjecture
            has been
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proven
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#Atiyah00"} Atiyah 2000
            %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#Atiyah01"} 01
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 4
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#EastwoodNorbury01"} Eastwood &amp; Norbury 01
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Atiyah-Sutcliffe+conjecture#AtiyahMalkoun18"} Atiyah &amp; Malkoun 18
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#OccurrencesAndApplications Occurrences and Applications
          %h3#compactification Compactification
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fulton-MacPherson+compactification"} Fulton-MacPherson compactification
            of configuration spaces of points in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            serves to exhibit them as models for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+n-disk+operad"} little n-disk operad
          %h3#stable_splitting_of_mapping_spaces Stable splitting of mapping spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+splitting+of+mapping+spaces"} stable splitting of mapping spaces
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
            of suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            are equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sums"} wedge sums
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectra"} suspension spectra
            of configuration spaces of points.
          %h3#correlators_as_differential_forms_on_configuration_spaces Correlators as differential forms on configuration spaces
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+field+theory"} Euclidean field theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            are often regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions+of+several+variables"} distributions of several variables
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+diagonal"} fat diagonal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-singular+distributions"} non-singular distributions
            after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+of+distributions"} restriction of distributions
            to the corresponding configuration space of points.
          %p
            For more on this see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators+as+differential+forms+on+configuration+spaces+of+points"} correlators as differential forms on configuration spaces of points
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group-completed+configuration+space+of+points"} group-completed configuration space of points
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+scheme"} Hilbert scheme
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrangements+of+hyperplanes"} arrangements of hyperplanes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+stability"} representation stability
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group"} braid group
            regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of a configuration space of points is considered (neither of them under these names, though) already in:
          %ul
            %li#Hurwitz1891
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adolf+Hurwitz"}> Adolf Hurwitz
              , §II of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Über Riemann’sche Flächen mit gegebenen Verzweigungspunkten
              %strong 39
              (1891) 1–60 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01199469"}> doi:10.1007/BF01199469
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            there regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action"} acting
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            forming
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branched+covers"} branched covers
          %p The concept of configuration spaces is then re-discovered/re-vived by:
          %ul
            %li#FadellNeuwirth62
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Fadell"}> Edward Fadell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lee+Neuwirth"} Lee Neuwirth
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Configuration spaces
                %strong 10
                (1962) 111-118 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.7146/math.scand.a-10517"}> doi:10.7146/math.scand.a-10517
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FadellNeuwirth-ConfigSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=141126"} MR141126
            %li#FoxNeuwirth62
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+H.+Fox"}> Ralph H. Fox
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lee+Neuwirth"} Lee Neuwirth
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The braid groups
                %strong 10
                (1962) 119-126
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.7146/math.scand.a-10518"}> doi:10.7146/math.scand.a-10518
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mscand.dk/article/view/10518/8539"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FoxNeuwirth-BraidGroups.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=150755"} MR150755
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (focus on the resulting
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+groups"} braid groups
          %p
            See also early occurences in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesInQuantumFieldTheory"} below
          %p General accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Fadell"}> Edward Fadell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sufian+Husseini"} Sufian Husseini
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometry and topology of configuration spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-56446-8"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-56446-8
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2002k:55038"} MR2002k:55038
            %li#Cohen09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frederick+R.+Cohen"}> Frederick R. Cohen
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to configuration spaces and their applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Braids
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 19
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814291415_0003"} doi:10.1142/9789814291415_0003
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/7550"} doi:10.1142/7550
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mimuw.edu.pl/~sjack/prosem/Cohen_Singapore.final.24.december.2008.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cohen-IntroConfigSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"}> Neil Strickland
                , section 3 of:
                %em A Bestiary of Topological Objects
                [
                %a{:href => "https://strickland1.org/courses/bestiary/bestiary.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Strickland-BestiaryTopological.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Craig+Westerland"}> Craig Westerland
                ,
                %em Configuration spaces in geometry and topology
                (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.austms.org.au/Publ/Gazette/2011/Nov11/TechPaperWesterland.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %li#Knudsen18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Knudsen"}> Ben Knudsen
                ,
                %em Configuration spaces in algebraic topology
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.11165"}> arXiv:1803.11165
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %li#Williams20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lucas+Williams"}> Lucas Williams
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Configuration Spaces for the Working Undergraduate
                %strong 21
                1 (2020) Article 8 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.11186"}> arXiv:1911.11186
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://scholar.rose-hulman.edu/rhumj/vol21/iss1/8"} rhumj:vol21/iss1/8
            %li#Kallel24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sadok+Kallel"}> Sadok Kallel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Configuration spaces of points: A user’s guide
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
                %strong 4
                (2025) 98-135 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.11092"}> arXiv:2407.11092
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-323-95703-8.00211-1"} doi:10.1016/B978-0-323-95703-8.00211-1
          %p
            In relation to
            = succeed ":" do
